error[ffi_const_field]: `fixedbugs-2388-const-in-an-element.h` declares `Deep`'s member `k` as `const`, inside an element of one of `Deep`'s array members, so C still refuses to assign any `Deep` — and this line is that assignment
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2388-a-const-member-two-arrays-deep-is-told.hero:25:19
     |
  25 |     built: Deep = Deep(n: 1, rest: zero)  #~ ffi_const_field
     |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: C11 counts a `const` member inside an array's element as it counts one at the top (C11 §6.3.2.1p1), though clang assigns it without a word: take one FROM the library through a pointer a function the group declares returns, rather than build it or receive it by value here

